{
  "about": "Third set for the planner comparison (financial_analyst_agent.planner_evaluation), held out for the run of 2026-10-03 and a development set since: that run's results were read, and one label (see label_changes) and the recorded SEC data changed after it. The fourth held-out set, planner-cases-held-out-4.json, replaced it. Written and labelled blind: from the product rules (period windows, company name forms, follow-up add versus replace, ordinary-word company names, ADR 0004 ambiguous metrics, refusals) before any planner was run on these cases, without reading earlier held-out sets or planner code. Same format and label semantics as planner-cases.json: each case is a conversation, its expectations apply to the last turn, and fields a case leaves out are not scored. A window in years counts 4 quarters per year, 'past year' is 4, 'a few' and 'several' are 4, months are a third rounded up; 'add/include/also X' adds companies and 'what about/how about/same for X' replaces them, keeping metric and window. Alphabet is labelled GOOG, as in planner-cases.json.",
  "label_changes": [
    {"id": "h3_amgn_two_metrics", "change": "outcome clarify -> answer with both metrics", "why": "Labelled from ADR 0004, which then said two catalog metrics in one question clarify. The product answers both, and the owner decided after the held-out run that answering both is right; ADR 0004 now says so."}
  ],
